Declare the mirror backend as a service entry point.

Upstream ships MirrorBackend.qml only as Panel.qml's private engine, so nothing
else can host it. OmaHub loads the same engine to render the device list inside
its Phone tab; without a service entry point the shell will not load it at all.

Purely additive: a plugin running standalone behaves exactly as before.
Proposed upstream; drop this patch once it lands.

--- a/manifest.json
+++ b/manifest.json
@@ -7,10 +7,12 @@
   "license": "MIT",
   "description": "Mirror and control your Android phone from the Omarchy bar: USB or Wi-Fi, keyboard and mouse, low latency, no root. A native panel over adb + scrcpy.",
   "kinds": [
-    "bar-widget"
+    "bar-widget",
+    "service"
   ],
   "entryPoints": {
-    "barWidget": "Panel.qml"
+    "barWidget": "Panel.qml",
+    "service": "MirrorBackend.qml"
   },
   "barWidget": {
     "displayName": "Android Mirror",
